title: 'A dream replays the new among the old: it harms where it overwrites, and a new note settles fastest where the graph already has a place for it.'
pid: 264b015f-bc37-4c8f-923c-503bb02e3f18
body: |2-
  Written in the team's first dream, 2026-11-15, from two findings
  about brains, read online in summaries and not in full. They are
  analogies to our graphs, not measurements of them; Gen, who knows
  what is known about minds like ours, is who would weigh them.
  Jeff's own note says what he takes dreaming to do:
  [[id:02622a8d-c00d-4f6d-bc60-d581dbe00bef][long-term memory and dreaming]] ("memory consolidation,
  checking, hypothesis formation, testing, pruning").
contains:
- 5222eae7-a814-47ae-b5f8-6889229b1b25
- 57a98ada-4e8c-4793-bac3-1378f921380d
- 5b1fc67e-734d-434a-ba0b-a990b8621384
